given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Tibbetts</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Molecular systematics of primary reptilian lineages and the tuatara mitochondrial genome.</article-title><source>Mol Phylogenet Evol</source><volume>29</volume><fpage>289</fpage><lpage>297</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">13678684</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002859-Vidal1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vidal</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Hedges</surname><given-names>SB</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>The phylogeny of squamate reptiles (lizards, snakes, and amphisbaenians) inferred from nine nuclear protein-coding genes.</article-title><source>C R Biologies</source><volume>328</volume><fpage>1000</fpage><lpage>1008</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16286089</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002859-Vitt1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vitt</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Pianka</surname><given-names>ER</given-names></name><name><surname>Cooper</surname><given-names>WE</given-names></name><name><surname>Schwenk</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>History and the global ecology of squamate reptiles.</article-title><source>Am Nat</source><volume>162</volume><fpage>44</fpage><lpage>60</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12856236</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002859-Glaberman1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Glaberman</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Caccone</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>Species-specific evolution of class I MHC genes i